WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.280
The first wave of series slated to debut on the&nbsp;
Disney+ streaming service promise the return of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.640
fan favorites and big-screen staples, bringing&nbsp;
some MCU adventure straight to your living room.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:16.120
But one show in particular is set apart by an&nbsp;
air of mystery and a strange title: What If...?

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.480
For quite some time now, we've all&nbsp;
been asking two important questions:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:25.040
"what if" and "when?" Well, we definitely&nbsp;
know the answer to the latter. On July 8,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:29.680
2021, Marvel dropped the first official&nbsp;
trailer for their new series and promised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.160
that the show would start streaming on August&nbsp;
11. For those without their calendars nearby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.040
that's a Wednesday — a tradition that was started&nbsp;
with the first episode of "Loki" back in June. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:44.640
taking a cue from the God of Mischief, all Disney+&nbsp;
MCU series will air on Wednesday going forward.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.920
As for how many episodes we can expect, in 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:53.280
ComicBook.com reported that Kevin Feige said&nbsp;
we're getting 10 episodes for Season 1. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:58.080
prepare yourself for the 10-episode&nbsp;
series to kick off on August 11.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:03.201
"I want it! Come on, gimme it.&nbsp;
Gimme it. Come on, give me it."

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:09.520
At the D23 Expo in 2019, Bryan Andrews was&nbsp;
announced as the director of "What If...?." You&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.400
may not have heard of him, but he's someone with&nbsp;
an impressive MCU history. Andrews worked in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.440
art department drawing storyboards for "Ant-Man,"&nbsp;
"Doctor Strange," and "Avengers: Endgame." "What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:24.800
If...?" will mark his first directing credit in 20&nbsp;
years, since directing the animated series "Jackie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:29.920
Chan Adventures" in 2001. Andrews is widely&nbsp;
known for his work on "Samurai Jack," which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:36.560
earned him two Emmys for Outstanding Individual&nbsp;
Achievement In Animation in 2005 and 2017.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.120
A.C. Bradley serves as the lead writer on "What&nbsp;
If...?" and has a relatively short résumé in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:46.800
the business. Bradley wrote one episode of&nbsp;
"Arrow" in 2014, in addition to 23 episodes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:53.200
of Netflix's "Trollhunters: Tales of Arcadia"&nbsp;
and 26 episodes of "3Below: Tales of Arcadia."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:59.040
As is normal with any MCU project, Kevin Feige&nbsp;
serves as an executive producer. Additionally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.560
Laura Karpman was tapped to create the&nbsp;
score for the "What If...?" episodes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:07.825
The composer has worked on the critically&nbsp;
acclaimed HBO series "Lovecraft Country."

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.408
Something MCU fans were delighted to&nbsp;
hear when "What If...?" was announced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.408 --> 00:02:14.400
was the confirmation that almost&nbsp;
every actor we know and love from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.760
the universe would be voicing the&nbsp;
characters they portray onscreen.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:22.800
Sadly, that doesn't include Robert Downey Jr., who&nbsp;
will not be returning, with someone else voicing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:28.000
Tony Stark instead. And at the time of this video,&nbsp;
Benedict Cumberbatch, Chris Evans, and Scarlett&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:33.280
Johansson aren't confirmed in the series to voice&nbsp;
their characters of Doctor Strange, Steve Rogers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.920
and Black Widow, even though we know those&nbsp;
characters are returning in some form or another.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.880
At the same time, rumors suggest there will be&nbsp;
an exciting story surrounding Natasha Romanoff.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:47.360
Who ends up voicing these characters will be quite&nbsp;
the surprise when their respective episodes air.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:53.920
One of the first big reveals that came with the&nbsp;
"What If...?" official announcement at SDCC 2019&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.800
was the identity of the series' narrator. For&nbsp;
10 episodes, "Westworld" star Jeffrey Wright&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.680
will lend his voice to the series as Uatu, the&nbsp;
Watcher. We got our first look at Uatu, who's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:09.040
a mysterious bald being who resembles a man, in&nbsp;
the Disney+ featurette "Expanding the Universe."

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:13.280
We know from the comics that Uatu is a part&nbsp;
of an ancient race known as the Watchers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:19.840
who simply observe all events throughout history.&nbsp;
First appearing in 1963's "Fantastic Four" #13,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:24.560
the Watchers' goal was to help less evolved&nbsp;
species since they were so technically advanced.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:28.800
After sharing nuclear technology with the&nbsp;
people of another planet, the population&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:33.840
decimated themselves, prompting the Watchers&nbsp;
to never intervene with civilizations again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.360
Wright, known for his smooth voice,&nbsp;
will voice Uatu as he watches over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:41.280
these what-could-have-been events on Earth&nbsp;
that involve many of our favorite heroes.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:47.520
The "What If" comics have been around since the&nbsp;
'70s, with the first issue kicking off in 1977.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:52.880
"What If" #1 had the subtitle "What If Spider-Man&nbsp;
Had Joined the Fantastic Four?" and started a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:58.720
successful run of alternate storylines with famous&nbsp;
characters. The volumes are also narrated by Uatu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:03.040
who, at the beginning of the issue, details&nbsp;
canonical events readers are familiar with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:08.080
and then introduces a "what if" moment that&nbsp;
changes the story entirely. The rest of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:13.040
issue follows that new alternate story, as&nbsp;
Uatu continues to narrate what never was.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:16.080
The upcoming television show&nbsp;
looks to be using the basic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:20.160
concept of the comic series with&nbsp;
the added twist of an MCU focus.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:24.880
Expect to see familiar moments from your favorite&nbsp;
Marvel movies twisted by one important change.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:30.000
Season 1 of "What If...?" will consist of&nbsp;
10 episodes, which doesn't seem like enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.400
room to explore all the possibilities&nbsp;
inherent in the premise. Unsurprisingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:39.520
a second season has already been confirmed.&nbsp;
In a 2019 interview with BuzzFeed Brasil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:44.080
Kevin Feige confirmed that the "What&nbsp;
If...?" series would go beyond 10 episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:47.360
and he's very excited at what&nbsp;
the studio has put together.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:51.760
"I'm very happy that we're doing a 'What If...?'&nbsp;
series for Disney+ right now, and I've seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:56.720
most of them. We have 10 for Season 1. We're&nbsp;
already working on the next ten for Season 2."

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:02.160
This is the first MCU Disney+ series to confirm&nbsp;
a second season, and it seems like the show could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:07.280
go even further past that. As the MCU evolves&nbsp;
and more characters are introduced to us on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:12.720
big screen, it opens the door to even more "What&nbsp;
If" comics storylines the studio can draw from.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:18.960
Here's one thing that we know 100% right out of&nbsp;
the gate — Episode 1 will follow Peggy Carter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:22.640
voiced by Hayley Atwell. Feige&nbsp;
also told BuzzFeed Brasil,

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:26.720
"We've revealed one that is very exciting.&nbsp;
We've talked about it for years, which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:31.200
the one where Peggy Carter gets the Super&nbsp;
Soldier serum and becomes Captain Carter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:35.920
That's the very first episode, and I'm excited&nbsp;
for people to see that. I'm excited to see the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:39.120
finished version of that, and I'm&nbsp;
excited for the world to see it."

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:44.880
Also detailed in the "What If...?" trailers&nbsp;
is a battle between two Doctor Stranges. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:49.440
particular episode will follow what would have&nbsp;
happened if there was an evil Sorcerer Supreme,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:53.200
but we expect the plot to have a much&nbsp;
more precise point of divergence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.200
which causes the shift in the story.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:06:00.320
We suspect this particular episode will&nbsp;
pull partly from "What If?" Vol. 1 #18,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:05.600
where Doctor Strange becomes a disciple&nbsp;
of Dormammu. Released in 1979, the comic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:10.560
follows an arrogant Stephen Strange whose hands&nbsp;
are healed by Baron Mordo through black magic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:15.680
Mordo works for the interdimensional being as his&nbsp;
follower, and he introduces Strange to the baddie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:19.440
The story takes Doctor Strange through&nbsp;
a long journey through self-discovery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:23.280
which he finds much quicker in the&nbsp;
character's introductory MCU film.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:29.200
Before his untimely death in 2020, Chadwick&nbsp;
Boseman participated in "What If...?" by lending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:33.840
his voice to T'Challa. There are a few glimpses&nbsp;
of the Wakandan in the trailer for the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:36.560
and it looks like this retelling&nbsp;
will imagine what would happen if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:41.120
the Ravagers from "Guardians of the Galaxy"&nbsp;
kidnapped T'Challa from Earth and not Peter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:45.600
Quill. Instead of becoming Black Panther,&nbsp;
T'Challa would take on the role of Star-Lord,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:48.640
eventually leading the Ravagers,&nbsp;
according to The Illuminerdi.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:50.020
"Who?"

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:53.920
"Star-Lord, man. Legendary outlaw?"

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:58.400
This won't be the only appearance of T'Challa&nbsp;
in "What If...?," however. Kevin Feige revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:03.280
to "Emmy Magazine" that Boseman came into the&nbsp;
studio and recorded his voice for four different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:08.720
episodes, so we can expect multiple MCU heroes&nbsp;
to pop up more than once in the animated series.

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:12.880
We're also going to be getting a&nbsp;
zombified version of Steve Rogers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:17.600
according to released footage. Taking down this&nbsp;
Captain America terror will be his best buddy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:21.360
Bucky Barnes, whose mission is to&nbsp;
prevent the spread of this zombie virus.

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:25.440
It should be noted that there are no zombie&nbsp;
storylines in the "What If" comics, but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:31.600
undead did have a run on the Marvel pages in 2005.&nbsp;
"Marvel Zombies" Vol. 1 was a limited series that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:37.280
saw the entire superhero population zombified, and&nbsp;
they subsequently ate the entire human race. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:42.240
have since been other volumes and spins on the&nbsp;
five-story series, all equally as gruesome. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:46.800
there is no apparent connection between zombie&nbsp;
Cap and living Bucky, it'll be exciting to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:51.840
how this story plays out on "What If...?" and what&nbsp;
event this deviated from in the duo's history.

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:57.280
T'Challa won't be the only nod to Wakanda in&nbsp;
"What If...?" In the series' official trailer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:02.160
we witness a young Killmonger save Tony Stark&nbsp;
from the missile that blows up in the original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:07.520
"Iron Man." We then watch as Killmonger rides on&nbsp;
a rhino and seemingly fights in a war for Wakanda.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:11.680
However, this time, it appears that Killmonger&nbsp;
will be the rightful heir to the throne.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:16.240
According to "ScreenRant," a toy leak has&nbsp;
revealed a Funko Pop figure that displays the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:20.960
"Black Panther" villain as king of Wakanda, but&nbsp;
it's not just his new title that's shocking. He's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:25.440
holding a blade in one hand and the severed head&nbsp;
of what's suspected to be Ultron in the other.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:29.040
We can't wait to see how this one plays&nbsp;
out and what scenario could have caused&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:33.760
an instance where Killmonger and Ultron&nbsp;
came face to face. In the MCU, "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:38.480
Age of Ultron" and "Black Panther" are set a year&nbsp;
apart, with the vengeful AI getting destroyed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:43.680
before we took a trip to Wakanda. Killmonger was&nbsp;
obviously around at the time of Ultron's creation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:48.560
just a bit younger, and it seems likely that he&nbsp;
sought out the AI once he learned of its creation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:53.680
by Tony Stark and Bruce Banner. If he is a force&nbsp;
for good and a strong king of Wakanda remains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:57.520
to be seen, but it would be a nice twist&nbsp;
to see him as a hero and not the villain.

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:01.920
The series' official trailer delivered&nbsp;
all sorts of superhero goodness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:06.880
and while we aren't exactly sure where the series&nbsp;
is headed, we're definitely excited to find out.

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:11.760
For example, at one point, we see Thor fighting&nbsp;
off Ultron's legions ... in Las Vegas of all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:16.560
place. We're assuming this might be connected to&nbsp;
some interesting merch details that were leaked in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:22.800
April 2021. According to "CBR," there's evidently&nbsp;
an official T-shirt and hat that both bear the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:27.600
image of "Party Thor." While there are more than a&nbsp;
handful of Thor stories from the "What If" comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:31.120
nothing seems to fall in line with&nbsp;
whoever the heck Party Thor is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:34.160
No matter what this story is&nbsp;
about, it's going to be a riot.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:38.960
The trailer also shows us a young Shuri in&nbsp;
action, Spider-Man arriving on the scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:43.120
Ego the Living Planet giving us a villainous&nbsp;
grin, and the return of Howard the Duck.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:44.660
"Gross."

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:52.800
On top of all that, it appears that Clint&nbsp;
Barton has somehow received a heavy dose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:58.080
of gamma radiation as it appears Hawkeye is&nbsp;
turning into the Hulk. It also looks like Loki&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:02.160
is leading an army of Asgardians against&nbsp;
Earth, and perhaps most interestingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:07.760
there's a shot of Thor, Black Panther, Star-Lord,&nbsp;
and Gamora holding Thanos' double-bladed sword&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:11.600
striking an "Avengers"-style pose&nbsp;
in the middle of a desolated city.

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:15.360
As for Thanos' favorite daughter, we've&nbsp;
definitely heard some interesting theories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:20.240
about her character. According to The Illuminerdi,&nbsp;
Gamora's storyline may follow her as she tracks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:24.160
down her new enemy — Tony Stark. This&nbsp;
plot point hasn't been confirmed yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:27.520
but if that does indeed pan out,&nbsp;
that would be a fascinating twist.

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:32.160
Last but not least, as we previously mentioned,&nbsp;
Natasha Romanoff is showing up in the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:36.560
alongside some version of the Hulk. And&nbsp;
according to another Illuminerdi report,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:41.040
this episode will allegedly see Black Widow&nbsp;
as one of the only survivors after Ultron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:46.080
successfully destroyed Earth in 2015.&nbsp;
No matter how crazy these stories seem,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:49.920
"What If...?" is going to be one of&nbsp;
the most unique MCU properties to date.

